cal order of their names (as guaranteed by ConcurrentSkipListMap).', 'description': 'Create a Zone with origin "example.com." and add RRsets for "a.example.com.", "z.example.com.", and "m.example.com.". Verify that toMasterFile() outputs the origin node first and the other three nodes in the order a, m, z.'}]}, {'group': 'Null origin leads to NPE', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NullPointerException is thrown because origin is null and the method calls origin.equals(entry.getKey()).', 'description': 'Create a Zone but never set its origin (origin remains null). Add any RRset (e.g., for "test.example.com."). Calling toMasterFile() should result in a NullPointerException.'}]}, {'group': 'Invalid originNode type', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'ClassCastException is thrown because originNode is set to an object of an unexpected type and nodeToString attempts to cast it to the internal node representation.', 'description': 'Create a Zone, set a valid origin (e.g., "example.com."), then use reflection to assign a String instance to the private field \'originNode\'. Calling toMasterFile() should propagate a ClassCastException from nodeToString.'}]}, {'group': 'Invalid data map value type', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'ClassCastException is thrown because a map entry value is of an incompatible type and nodeToString attempts to process it.', 'description': "Create a Zone with a valid origin, then use reflection to put an entry into the private 'data' map where the key is a proper Name instance but the value is a plain Integer. When toMasterFile() iterates over the map, nodeToString will receive the Integer and throw a ClassCastException."}]}, {'group': 'Null key in data map', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NullPointerException is thrown when origin.equals(entry.getKey()) is evaluated because the map contains a null key.', 'description': "Create a Zone with a non‑null origin, then use reflection to insert a null key with any non‑null value into the